  "body": "Found by the context read for #3694 (the same defect in the Haas post).\n\n## What happens\n\nEach of these post scripts writes a mm feed as a whole number (`Math.round`): `fanuc`, `doosan-dnm`, `mazak`, `sinumerik`, `tormach`, `linuxcnc`. The tap feed is pitch x spindle speed (`crates/motion/src/drilling/cycle.rs:33`), and the stream keeps 0.001 mm/min. The post rounds it. Example: M1.4 x 0.3 at S115 has the exact feed 34.5; the post writes `F35`. The pitch that the control cuts is F / S, so the pitch is wrong by 1.45 percent.\n\nNot affected, by the same read: `mach4` (one decimal; check that one decimal is sufficient), `fanuc-lathe` (feed for each revolution, four decimals), `heidenhain` (refuses a pitch that it cannot write).\n\n## Expected\n\nThe F word of a tapping block gives the exact feed for the pitch and the speed, or the post refuses the pair by name.\n\n## Done means\n\n- A test for each of the six posts pins the tapping F word for 34.5 and 133.2 mm/min.\n- The format of the F word obeys the decimal point rule of each control (#3690).\n- `mach4` is checked with a feed that needs three decimals.\n\nRefs #3694, #3690, #3692.\n",
